Chap1 Encapsulation
Constructor in Encapsulation
A constructor is a special function in a class:  
Same name as the class.  
Not have a return value.  
It is automatically called when an object is created (the programmer does not call it directly).  
If no constructor is declared, the program automatically provides a default empty constructor. 
⇒ What is the access modifier for the default constructor?  ⇒ Can we create a private constructor? (Singleton Pattern)
