public class Getset {
private int age;
// Getter for 'age'
public int getAge() {
return age;
}
// Setter for 'age' with validation
public void setAge(int age) {
if (age >= 0) {
this.age = age;
} else {
System.out.println("Age cannot be negative.");
}
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
}
}
Getters and Setters are methods used to access and modify the private fields of a class, adhering to the principles of encapsulation
